The invention relates to a process for producing a purified gas stream from a feed gas stream comprising contaminants, the process comprising the following steps:
(a) removing contaminants from the feed gas stream to obtain the purified gas stream and a sour gas stream comprising hydrogen sulphide and mercaptans;
(b) separating the sour gas stream comprising hydrogen sulphide and mercaptans into a gas stream enriched in hydrogen sulphide and a residual gas stream comprising mercaptans;
(c) converting hydrogen sulphide in the gas stream enriched in hydrogen sulphide to elemental sulphur in a Claus unit, thereby obtaining a first off-gas stream comprising sulphur dioxide;
(d) converting sulphur dioxide in the first off-gas stream comprising sulphur dioxide to hydrogen sulphide in a Claus off-gas treating reactor to obtain a second off-gas stream comprising hydrogen sulphide;
(e) converting mercaptans from the residual gas stream comprising mercaptans to hydrogen sulphide in a mercaptans conversion reactor to obtain a residual gas stream comprising hydrogen sulphide,
wherein step (e) comprises contacting the residual gas stream comprising mercaptans with a hydrogenation catalyst comprising nickel and molybdenum or nickel and tungsten supported on a carrier, in the presence of hydrogen, at a temperature in the range of 260 to 350 °C.

A respiratory assistance apparatus (10) configured to provide a heated and humidified gases stream, comprising:
a gases inlet configured to receive a supply of gases;
a blower unit configured to generate a pressurised gases stream from the supply of gases;
a humidification unit (14) configured to heat and humidify the pressurised gases stream;
a gases outlet for the heated and humidified gases stream;
a flow path (54,56) for the gases stream through the respiratory device from the gases inlet through the blower unit and humidification unit to the gases outlet;
a sensor assembly (60) provided in the flow path before the humidification unit, the sensor assembly comprising an ultrasound gas composition sensor system for sensing one or more gas concentrations within the gases stream.

A respiratory assistance (10) apparatus configured to provide a heated and humidified gases stream, comprising:
a main housing (26,28) comprising:
a gases inlet(s) configured to receive one or more gases to form a gases stream;
a blower unit configured to pressurise the gases stream;
a humidification unit (15) configured to heat and humidify the gases stream;
a gases outlet (12) following the blower unit and humidification unit for the gases stream; and
a sensor assembly (60) in a flow path (54,56) of the main housing, the sensor assembly comprising a sensor housing that is a modular component and releasably mounted within the flow path, and wherein the sensor housing comprises an ultrasound gas composition sensor system for sensing one or more gas concentrations within the gases stream.

A method for preparing a PAEK powder for use in SLS includes the steps of:
providing a raw, non-powder PAEK material, optionally comprising one or more liquid solvents;
after the providing step, heat treating the raw PAEK to evaporate at least substantially all of any liquid solvent in the raw PAEK, causing at least substantially all of the raw PAEK to be in the form of irregularly-shaped particles;
after the heat treating step, cooling the raw PAEK; and
after the cooling step, grinding the raw PAEK to form a PAEK powder.
